IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ec59-nouns`
IMPORT `ec59-cross-references`

-- Row il-59. The controls hold, the record of the old name holds, and the recorded facts about the four defects are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their eight failing assertions are in ec59-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in ec59-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound controls`

-- Control for items 2 and 3: fee item (a)(1) names an application to approve a restrictive arrangement under section 7, and section 7 is that application.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: fee item (a)(1) to section 7`)
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: fee item (a)(1) to section 7`)
#ASSERT `the target holds the kind of proceeding the citing words name` (`reference: fee item (a)(1) to section 7`)
-- Control for item 4: the notice before it prints the index of November 2022 against the index of November 2021, one year apart.
#ASSERT `the earlier index is the one of the year before the later index` (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 10454, p. 598`)
#ASSERT `years between the two indexes printed` (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 10454, p. 598`) EQUALS 1
-- Control for item 5: the Schedule's note names regulation 2, and regulation 2 is printed.
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: the Schedule's note to regulation 2 of the 1964 regulations`)
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: the Schedule's note to regulation 2 of the 1964 regulations`)

§ `Tests of item 1: the old name in printed titles (a record, not a defect)`

-- The rename: the instrument replaces the words of the old name by the words of the new name.
#ASSERT (`rename: section 1 of Sefer HaChukim 2781, p. 246`)'s `it replaces` EQUALS `the words the 2019 rename replaced: ההגבלים העסקיים`
#ASSERT (`rename: section 1 of Sefer HaChukim 2781, p. 246`)'s `by` EQUALS `the words the 2019 rename put in their place: התחרות הכלכלית`
-- The Law's own title, as the consolidation prints it, carries the new name.
#ASSERT (`title: the Law, as its consolidation prints it`)'s `the title carries` EQUALS `the words the 2019 rename put in their place: התחרות הכלכלית`
#ASSERT NOT `the title carries the old name` (`title: the Law, as its consolidation prints it`)
-- Four titles of instruments under the Law carry the old name: the annual notice (official crop) and three others (consolidation only).
#ASSERT `the title carries the old name` (`title: the annual fee notice printed in KT 12149, p. 482`)
#ASSERT `the title carries the old name` (`title: the fee regulations of 1989`)
#ASSERT `the title carries the old name` (`title: the police-station order of 2000`)
#ASSERT `the title carries the old name` (`title: the 1964 regulations`)
#ASSERT `the number of recorded instruments under the Law whose title carries the old name` EQUALS 4
-- Where each was read from.
#ASSERT (`title: the annual fee notice printed in KT 12149, p. 482`)'s `the title was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`title: the fee regulations of 1989`)'s `the title was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`title: the police-station order of 2000`)'s `the title was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`title: the 1964 regulations`)'s `the title was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`title: the Law, as its consolidation prints it`)'s `the title was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`

§ `Tests of what the records of the four defects say`

-- Item 2, fee item (a)(3) and section 28.
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `section 28 of the Law, as fee item (a)(3) names it: an appeal against a requirement of the Commissioner`
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `section 28 of the Law, as its consolidation prints it: a repeal marker in place of text`
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)'s `the consolidation prints the named text as repealed` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)
#ASSERT NOT `the target holds the kind of proceeding the citing words name` (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)
-- Item 3, fee item (b)(5) and section 30: the consolidation prints section 30 as in force, but without an application of the kind the item names.
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `section 30 of the Law, as fee item (b)(5) names it: an application to regulate monopoly actions`
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `section 30 of the Law, as its consolidation prints it: instructions of the Commissioner to a monopolist, and an objection to the Tribunal in subsection (ו)`
#ASSERT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)
#ASSERT NOT `the target holds the kind of proceeding the citing words name` (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)
-- Item 4, the two years as printed: 2023 against 2021, two years apart.
#ASSERT (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 11002, p. 948`)'s `the year of the later index printed` EQUALS 2023
#ASSERT (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 11002, p. 948`)'s `the year of the earlier index printed` EQUALS 2021
#ASSERT `years between the two indexes printed` (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 11002, p. 948`) EQUALS 2
-- Item 5, the 1964 regulations and section 10א of the 1959 Law.
#ASSERT (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `section 10א of the 1959 Law, as the 1964 regulations name it: the source of the power to make them`
#ASSERT (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `the 1959 Law, as section 53 of the Law prints it: repealed`
#ASSERT (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)'s `the consolidation prints the named text as repealed` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the consolidation prints the named text as in force` (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)
-- Whether the 1964 regulations continue in force is not decided: the record holds NOTHING for the proceeding question.
#ASSERT (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)'s `the target holds a proceeding of the kind the citing words name` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- No reference here has both limbs read from the official instrument alone.
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instrument alone` (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instrument alone` (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instrument alone` (`reference: fee item (a)(1) to section 7`)
#ASSERT NOT `both limbs were read from the official instrument alone` (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)
-- Item 2: both limbs were read from a cropped page of an official instrument; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY.
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (a)(3) to section 28`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Item 3: limb (a) is the consolidation only (its amending instruments were not read); limb (b) is the cropped page.
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: fee item (b)(5) to section 30`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Item 5: both limbs are the consolidation only (the Kovetz HaTakanot issue of 1964 was not read).
#ASSERT (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: the 1964 regulations' power line to section 10א of the 1959 Law`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- Item 4: read from the cropped page of each notice.
#ASSERT (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 11002, p. 948`)'s `the recital was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`recital: Kovetz HaTakanot 10454, p. 598`)'s `the recital was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

